From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: defcom5-rockchip <286489597+defcom5-rockchip@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 20:35:39 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: aic8800: tdls_mgmt takes link_id on 6.1.189

Stable v6.1.189 backported the cfg80211_ops::tdls_mgmt link_id argument
(a5fcb2b18a7d; upstream since 6.5), and the vendor aic8800 SDIO driver has
no case for it, so it fails to build:

  rwnx_main.c: error: initialization of 'int (*)(struct wiphy *, struct
  net_device *, const u8 *, int, u8, u8, u16, u32, bool, const u8 *,
  size_t)' from incompatible pointer type

Add the argument for 6.5+ and for 6.1.189 up to 6.2, the same guard the
bcmdhd driver uses. The driver does not use it.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/aic8800_sdio/aic8800_fdrv/rwnx_main.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/aic8800_sdio/aic8800_fdrv/rwnx_main.c
@@ -5513,6 +5513,10 @@
 #else
 	u8 *peer,
 #endif
+#if LINUX_VERSION_CODE >= KERNEL_VERSION(6, 5, 0) || \
+	(LINUX_VERSION_CODE >= KERNEL_VERSION(6, 1, 189) && LINUX_VERSION_CODE < KERNEL_VERSION(6, 2, 0))
+	int link_id,
+#endif
 	u8 action_code,
 	u8 dialog_token,
 	u16 status_code,
